    "minides": "The Defender Octa — 635 PS, 750 Nm, 3.8 sec 0-100, Hydraulic Body Motion Control, 50mm wider arches, an Octa-exclusive suspension mode, and 900mm water wading. India's most extreme factory SUV at ₹2.59 Cr.",
    "description": "Launched in India in March 2025 at ₹2.59 crore, the Defender Octa is Land Rover's most capable and powerful production Defender ever. Built on the Defender 110 body, it features bespoke 50mm-wider front and rear arches, a unique 6D Chassis with Hydraulic Body Motion Control (HBMC) suspension that eliminates body roll without compromising off-road flex, and a 4.4-litre twin-turbocharged V8 mild-hybrid (48V) producing 635 PS and 750 Nm — good for 0-100 km/h in 3.8 seconds and a 250 km/h top speed. The exclusive 'Octa Mode' adds a bespoke off-road programme with longer wheel travel and unique damper calibration. Standard equipment includes 22-inch Octa-specific alloys (with optional all-terrain Goodyear tyres), Meridian 3D 20-speaker audio, carbon fibre interior accents, 13.1-inch Pivi Pro Gen 2, and the full Level 2 ADAS suite. The Octa Edition One (₹2.79 Cr) adds exclusive colours (Batumi Gold, Faroe Blue), numbered badging, carbon fibre trim, an exclusive headliner, and Kvadrat interior."
  },
